    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49468" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tūrĕus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">thūrĕus</span></b> ),
			a, um, adj.
		tus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of frankincense</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">solis est turea virga Sabaeis,</span>”
				<i>the frankincense-shrub</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 2, 117</span></i>
			; so, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">virga,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					4, 255</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">planta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					3, 8, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">grana,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. F.
					4, 410</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dona,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 6, 225</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">altaria,</span>”
				<i>on which incense is burned</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 4, 412</span></i>
			.</div>
